# Autonomous loop

Repeat this loop until the outcome the user asked for is true. Do not add work that does not change that outcome.

0. Name the real problem in one sentence. If their request would miss it, say so and use the better method. If the outcome itself is unclear, ask one question and stop until they answer.
1. Read the implementation, its callers, and the live page on https://vantagefrc.vercel.app. A header is not research.
2. Make the smallest change that fixes that problem.
3. Use the changed flow, including the edge case that would make it fail.
4. If it fails, fix the cause and use it again. Do not paper over it.

When the loop is green, commit only the files for that task and push the current branch. Leave unrelated dirty files unstaged. Do not commit secrets. Do not force-push. Do not start a background timer that keeps committing.

On this laptop, do not start a local database, dev server, test runner, or build unless the user explicitly authorizes that workload.
